<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>wasp-os builds</title>
<meta name="description" content="Firmware builds of wasp-os, the MicroPython smart watch OS, for the PineTime.">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>
<main>
<h1>wasp-os builds</h1>
<p class="lede">Firmware for the PineTime smart watch: wasp-os, the watch
operating system written in MicroPython.</p>

<section class="release">
<h2>Latest: {{version}}</h2>
<p class="meta">Built {{date}} from commit
<a href="{{commit_url}}">{{commit}}</a> &middot;
<a href="releases.json">releases.json</a></p>
{{notes}}
{{files}}
</section>

<h2>Companion</h2>
<p>Set the clock, the alarms and the watch face from Chrome or Edge, over
Bluetooth: <a href="companion/">open the companion</a>.</p>

<h2>Update a watch that runs wasp-os</h2>
<p>With <a href="{{source_url}}/tree/master/tools/wasptool">wasptool</a>, from a
checkout of the source:</p>
<pre>cd tools/wasptool
uv run wasptool update</pre>
<p>Your settings, alarms and step count are kept.</p>

<h2>Install wasp-os for the first time</h2>
<p>First install the wasp-os bootloader with one of the reloader files above,
then the firmware. The <a href="{{docs_url}}install.html">installation
guide</a> explains each way.</p>

{{older}}

<footer>
<p>These are builds of <a href="{{source_url}}">mbeijen/wasp-os</a>, a fork
with fixes that are not in the <a href="{{upstream_url}}">wasp-os project</a>
yet. They are not official wasp-os releases.</p>
</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
